As shown in Figs.  8 ,  9 ,  10 ,  11 ,  12 ,  14  and  15 , data representing post-fire response such as yield strength at different strain values, ultimate tensile strength, modulus of elasticity and hardness mostly follow similar trends. The changes in these properties can be accurately presented as a function of the temperature. By applying curve-fitting to the data presented in Figs.  8 ,  9 ,  10 ,  11 ,  12 ,  14  and  15 , Eq. ( 1 ) has been developed. This equation comprises a two-regime predictive model to represent the temperature-dependent evolution of post-fire mechanical response. The post-fire response is expressed as the product of a temperature-dependent residual factor and the corresponding room-temperature response (Response) AT : 1 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
